name:integrate-libssh2-candidate-adapter
ac:1. The M0-viability tier adapter builds from pinned source with the approved crypto backend for the macOS harness and macOS provider configuration and exposes no libssh2 type across the shared boundary. 2. Socket readiness and LIBSSH2_ERROR_EAGAIN are integrated without busy spinning or unbounded buffering, with deterministic cancellation and timeout behavior. 3. Raw host-key evidence before authentication, approved public-key auth, direct-tcpip, bidirectional exec, exec/stdin upload, client rekey, server-rekey handling, bounded buffers, keepalive, available metrics, Keychain-only secret references, and privacy-safe errors satisfy every M0-viability-mandatory row or remain red with reproducible evidence. 4. The four M3-deferred semantics are emitted as explicit not-reported or unsupported states and are traceable to TASK-260728-3cveay; no deferred value is fabricated. 5. Repeated connect and cancel smoke runs return sessions, channels, sockets, tasks, and custom allocations to baseline.
